    "title": "Recall petition against Leslie Mayor Corey Capone dismissed - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joshua Windus ,\n11 hours ago\nThe recall petition against Leslie Mayor Corey Capone was dismissed as legally insufficient on Nov. 5. The recall petition application was submitted more than 15 days after the sponsor received the application form.\nMayor Corey Capone declined comment after the decision.\nFormer Police Chief Bob Smith, who circulated and filed the petition, says he does not plan to refile. “I wish the mayor all the best in his time as mayor, hope he can take the judge’s advice and try to mend some of these issues that’s going on. Because, as the judge says, the general public doesn’t have any faith in him.”\nAdd to Preferred Sources\n1",
    "summary": "The recall petition against Leslie Mayor Corey Capone was dismissed as legally insufficient on Nov. 5. The recall petition application was submitted more than 15 days after the sponsor received the application form. Mayor Corey Capone declined comment after the decision. Former Police Chief Bob Smith, who circulated and filed the petition, says he does not plan to refile. Because, as the judge says, the general public doesn’t have any faith in him.”",
